    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But the legacy is just a ghost. It's for the people who are left behind, not for the one who lived it. I don't want to be a memory or a \"legend\" watching my hands shake and my mind turn to fog. There's a certain dignity in knowing exactly when the work is complete—to step away while the masterpiece is still intact, rather than letting it dissolve into a long, messy decay. Doesn't it seem more... intentional? To leave while the music is still perfect?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
